      "message": "Bazel Modules migration is still ongoing.\n\nWe still depend on Bazel 7.6.1 (`.bazelversion`).\n\nAfter removal of `WORKSPACE` (better to say, moving its content to WORKSPACE.bzlmod`) outdated `bazelisk` version would fail to detect `.bazelversion` file and use the latest available Bazel version (9.0.1 as of today).\n\nGiven that Bazel 9.x removed old `WORKSPACE` file support, hybrid mode we use today wouldn\u0027t work.\n\nUpdating Bazelisk to at least v.1.27.0 should fix it for you.\n\nSee also explanation the commit message of Zuul/jobs change 562881.\n\nYou can download the latest `bazelisk` version from GitHub release page: [1].\n\n[1]: https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazelisk/releases/tag/v1.28.1",
